{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "c87cc190-6b96-4807-83b0-988e7a76c86a",
    "name": "GK One Identity — QA (dev)",
    "description": "Exercises GK One Identity the way an integrating application does: the OAuth 2.1 authorization code flow with PKCE, and the endpoints a token opens.\n\nIt is pointed at the **dev** test client and needs nothing filled in.\n\n**Sign in.** Open the collection's **Authorization** tab and press **Get New Access Token**. Postman opens the GK One sign-in window, and the token comes back to it. Press **Use Token**. Nothing here posts a password to an internal endpoint: the sign-in happens where a customer's would.\n\nFolder `01` copies that token into the **accessToken** variable, for the requests that need the raw string. Folder `02` runs the same flow by hand when you want the refresh token captured too, which Postman's helper keeps to itself.\n\n**Not covered here.** The account pages, linked applications and signed-in sessions answer to a browser session cookie rather than to an access token, so they are tested at `/account` in a browser and not from Postman.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "19799427",
    "_collection_link": "https://go.postman.co/collection/19799427-c87cc190-6b96-4807-83b0-988e7a76c86a?source=collection_link"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "00 · Discovery",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Discovery document",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Answers 200 with no subscription key', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Advertises S256 and refuses plain', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.code_challenge_methods_supported).to.eql(['S256']);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Advertises RS256 signing', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.id_token_signing_alg_values_supported).to.include('RS256');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Advertises only the two grant types', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.grant_types_supported).to.have.members(['authorization_code', 'refresh_token']);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// The rest of the collection addresses whatever this document names, so a moved endpoint is picked",
                  "// up here rather than by every request failing on its own.",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('authorizeEndpoint', body.authorization_endpoint);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('tokenEndpoint', body.token_endpoint);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('userinfoEndpoint', body.userinfo_endpoint);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('introspectEndpoint', body.introspection_endpoint);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('jwksEndpoint', body.jwks_uri);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{issuer}}/.well-known/openid-configuration",
              "host": [
                "{{issuer}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                ".well-known",
                "openid-configuration"
              ]
            },
            "description": "What an integrator points an OIDC library at. Must answer without a subscription key."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "JWKS",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Answers 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Publishes at least one RS256 key with a kid', function () {",
                  "    const keys = pm.response.json().keys;",
                  "    pm.expect(keys).to.be.an('array').that.is.not.empty;",
                  "    pm.expect(keys[0]).to.have.property('kid');",
                  "    pm.expect(keys[0].alg).to.eql('RS256');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{issuer}}/jwks",
              "host": [
                "{{issuer}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "jwks"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The public keys a third party verifies an id_token against."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ],
      "description": "Run these first. They need no token, and they fill the endpoint variables the rest of the collection uses, so a moved endpoint shows up here instead of breaking every request below."
    },
    {
      "name": "01 · Signed in, through Postman's OAuth helper",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Userinfo, and capture the token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "// Postman holds the OAuth token in its own store. This copies it into accessToken so the",
                  "// requests below that need the raw string (introspect, and anything pasted elsewhere) can use it.",
                  "const sent = pm.request.headers.get('Authorization') || '';",
                  "const bearer = sent.replace(/^Bearer\\s+/i, '').trim();",
                  "",
                  "if (bearer) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', bearer);",
                  "}",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Answers 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Carries the claims the contract lists', function () {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('sub');",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('email');",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('sub', body.sub);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Access token was captured into the accessToken variable', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.collectionVariables.get('accessToken')).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "packages": {},
                "requests": {}
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{accessToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{issuer}}/userinfo",
              "host": [
                "{{issuer}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "userinfo"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Reads the signed-in customer back out of the token, and saves the token to the accessToken variable."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Introspect the access token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Answers 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Reports the access token as active', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().active).to.be.true;",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "packages": {},
                "requests": {}
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{accessToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{accessToken}}",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{issuer}}/introspect",
              "host": [
                "{{issuer}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "introspect"
              ]
            },
            "description": "RFC 7662. The endpoint is itself protected, so the bearer authorises the call and the form carries the token being asked about."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Introspect the id token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Answers 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "console.log('active:', pm.response.json().active);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "packages": {},
                "requests": {}
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{accessToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{idToken}}",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{issuer}}/introspect",
              "host": [
                "{{issuer}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "introspect"
              ]
            },
            "description": "An id_token is not an access token. Introspection should report it inactive."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ],
      "description": "Press **Get New Access Token** on the collection's Authorization tab, sign in, then **Use Token**. Run **Userinfo** first: it copies the token into the **accessToken** variable, for the requests that need the raw string."
    },
    {
      "name": "02 · Sign in by hand, to capture the refresh token",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Build the sign-in URL",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Builds a PKCE pair and the /authorize URL. Use this folder when you want the refresh token",
                  "// captured for you; the collection-level OAuth 2.0 helper does not hand it to a variable.",
                  "const verifier = CryptoJS.lib.WordArray.random(48)",
                  "    .toString(CryptoJS.enc.Base64)",
                  "    .replace(/\\+/g, '-').replace(/\\//g, '_').replace(/=/g, '');",
                  "",
                  "const challenge = CryptoJS.SHA256(verifier)",
                  "    .toString(CryptoJS.enc.Base64)",
                  "    .replace(/\\+/g, '-').replace(/\\//g, '_').replace(/=/g, '');",
                  "",
                  "const state = CryptoJS.lib.WordArray.random(16).toString(CryptoJS.enc.Hex);",
                  "const nonce = CryptoJS.lib.WordArray.random(16).toString(CryptoJS.enc.Hex);",
                  "",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('codeVerifier', verifier);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('state', state);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('nonce', nonce);",
                  "",
                  "const url = pm.collectionVariables.get('issuer') + '/authorize'",
                  "    + '?response_type=code'",
                  "    + '&client_id=' + encodeURIComponent(pm.collectionVariables.get('clientId'))",
                  "    + '&redirect_uri=' + encodeURIComponent(pm.collectionVariables.get('redirectUri'))",
                  "    + '&scope=' + encodeURIComponent(pm.collectionVariables.get('scope'))",
                  "    + '&code_challenge=' + challenge",
                  "    + '&code_challenge_method=S256'",
                  "    + '&state=' + state",
                  "    + '&nonce=' + nonce;",
                  "",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('authorizeUrl', url);",
                  "console.log('Open this in a browser, sign in, then copy the \"code\" from the address bar:');",
                  "console.log(url);"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Authorize URL built. Open it from the Postman console.', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.collectionVariables.get('authorizeUrl')).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "console.log('');",
                  "console.log('=== Sign-in URL ===');",
                  "console.log(pm.collectionVariables.get('authorizeUrl'));",
                  "console.log('');",
                  "console.log('Sign in, then paste the code from the address bar into the {{authCode}} variable');",
                  "console.log('and run \"Exchange code for tokens\".');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{issuer}}/.well-known/openid-configuration",
              "host": [
                "{{issuer}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                ".well-known",
                "openid-configuration"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Builds the PKCE pair and prints the authorize URL. The request itself is the discovery document, which keeps this from being a request to nowhere."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Exchange code for tokens",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Answers 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Returns an access token and an id token', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('access_token');",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('id_token');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', body.access_token || '');",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('idToken', body.id_token || '');",
                  "",
                  "// offline_access decides this one. Its absence is a pass where the scope was not asked for or the",
                  "// application is not allowed it: see the Session and token refresh milestone.",
                  "if (body.refresh_token) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', body.refresh_token);",
                  "    console.log('Refresh token captured.');",
                  "} else {",
                  "    console.log('No refresh token. Expected unless offline_access is both allowed and requested.');",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "packages": {},
                "requests": {}
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                {
                  "key": "grant_type",
                  "value": "authorization_code",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "code",
                  "value": "{{authCode}}",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "redirect_uri",
                  "value": "{{redirectUri}}",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "client_id",
                  "value": "{{clientId}}",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "client_secret",
                  "value": "{{clientSecret}}",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "code_verifier",
                  "value": "{{codeVerifier}}",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{issuer}}/token",
              "host": [
                "{{issuer}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "token"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Spends the authorization code with the verifier that matches the challenge sent at /authorize. Saves the access, id and refresh tokens."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh the access token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Answers 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Returns a new access token', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('access_token');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', body.access_token || '');",
                  "",
                  "// A rotated refresh token replaces the one just spent; without this the next refresh uses a dead one.",
                  "if (body.refresh_token) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', body.refresh_token);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                {
                  "key": "grant_type",
                  "value": "refresh_token",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "refresh_token",
                  "value": "{{refreshToken}}",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "client_id",
                  "value": "{{clientId}}",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "client_secret",
                  "value": "{{clientSecret}}",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{issuer}}/token",
              "host": [
                "{{issuer}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "token"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Needs offline_access allowed on the application and asked for in the scope. Saves the rotated refresh token over the one just spent."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ],
      "description": "Postman's OAuth helper keeps the refresh token to itself. This folder runs the same flow request by request so every token lands in a variable.\n\n1. Run **Build the sign-in URL**. It generates the PKCE pair and prints the URL to the Postman console.\n2. Open that URL in a browser and sign in.\n3. Copy the `code` from the address bar into the `authCode` variable.\n4. Run **Exchange code for tokens**."
    },
    {
      "name": "03 · Refusals",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Authorize without code_challenge",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// OAuth 2.1 requires PKCE on every authorization request. The server checks redirect_uri first, so",
                  "// an unregistered callback fails here for the wrong reason. That case is called out rather than",
                  "// passing quietly as \"it returned an error\".",
                  "const location = pm.response.headers.get('Location') || '';",
                  "const body = pm.response.text() || '';",
                  "const setupIncomplete = pm.response.code === 400 && /redirect_uri/i.test(body);",
                  "",
                  "if (setupIncomplete) {",
                  "    pm.test('SETUP NEEDED: register the Postman callback, then run this again', function () {",
                  "        pm.expect.fail(",
                  "            'The server refused the redirect_uri, so PKCE was never reached. Add ' +",
                  "            pm.collectionVariables.get('redirectUri') +",
                  "            ' under GK Identity -> Applications -> Redirect URIs.');",
                  "    });",
                  "} else {",
                  "    pm.test('Redirects the refusal back to the application', function () {",
                  "        pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(302);",
                  "    });",
                  "",
                  "    pm.test('Names invalid_request and issues no code', function () {",
                  "        pm.expect(location).to.include('error=invalid_request');",
                  "        pm.expect(location).to.not.include('code=');",
                  "    });",
                  "",
                  "    pm.test('Refuses before the sign-in screen', function () {",
                  "        pm.expect(location).to.not.include('/auth?');",
                  "    });",
                  "}",
                  "",
                  "console.log('Status:', pm.response.code, '| Location:', location || '(none)');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "protocolProfileBehavior": {
            "followRedirects": false
          },
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{issuer}}/authorize?response_type=code&client_id={{clientId}}&redirect_uri={{redirectUri}}&scope=openid&state=qa-no-pkce",
              "host": [
                "{{issuer}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "authorize"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "response_type",
                  "value": "code"
                },
                {
                  "key": "client_id",
                  "value": "{{clientId}}"
                },
                {
                  "key": "redirect_uri",
                  "value": "{{redirectUri}}"
                },
                {
                  "key": "scope",
                  "value": "openid"
                },
                {
                  "key": "state",
                  "value": "qa-no-pkce"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "OAuth 2.1 requires PKCE on every request. Redirects are not followed, so the refusal stays visible."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Authorize with an unregistered redirect_uri",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// An unregistered redirect_uri must never be redirected to, or the server is an open redirector.",
                  "// The refusal has to come back directly.",
                  "const location = pm.response.headers.get('Location') || '';",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Answers 400 rather than redirecting', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(400);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Does not redirect to the unregistered URI', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(location).to.not.include('evil.example');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Says the redirect_uri is the problem', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.match(/redirect_uri/i);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "protocolProfileBehavior": {
            "followRedirects": false
          },
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{issuer}}/authorize?response_type=code&client_id={{clientId}}&redirect_uri=https%3A%2F%2Fevil.example%2Fcallback&scope=openid&code_challenge=E9Melhoa2OwvFrEMTJguCHaoeK1t8URWbuGJSstw-cM&code_challenge_method=S256&state=qa-bad-redirect",
              "host": [
                "{{issuer}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "authorize"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "response_type",
                  "value": "code"
                },
                {
                  "key": "client_id",
                  "value": "{{clientId}}"
                },
                {
                  "key": "redirect_uri",
                  "value": "https%3A%2F%2Fevil.example%2Fcallback"
                },
                {
                  "key": "scope",
                  "value": "openid"
                },
                {
                  "key": "code_challenge",
                  "value": "E9Melhoa2OwvFrEMTJguCHaoeK1t8URWbuGJSstw-cM"
                },
                {
                  "key": "code_challenge_method",
                  "value": "S256"
                },
                {
                  "key": "state",
                  "value": "qa-bad-redirect"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "An unregistered URI must never be redirected to. The refusal comes back directly, or the server is an open redirector."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Token without code_verifier",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Answers 400', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(400);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Names invalid_request', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.eql('invalid_request');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                {
                  "key": "grant_type",
                  "value": "authorization_code",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "code",
                  "value": "{{authCode}}",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "redirect_uri",
                  "value": "{{redirectUri}}",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "client_id",
                  "value": "{{clientId}}",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "client_secret",
                  "value": "{{clientSecret}}",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{issuer}}/token",
              "host": [
                "{{issuer}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "token"
              ]
            },
            "description": "PKCE is not optional at the token endpoint either."
          },
          "response": []
